# GitHub Actions naming (Scheme A)

When adding or editing workflows under `.github/workflows/`:

1. Follow **Scheme A** in [`docs/runbooks/github-actions-naming.md`](docs/runbooks/github-actions-naming.md).
2. Display `name:` must be `"<Area>: <purpose>"` with Area in `{CI, CD, Ops, Search, Maint}`.
3. New workflow **filenames** should use `<area>-<purpose>[-cadence].yml` (`ci-`, `cd-`, `ops-`, `search-`, `maint-`).
4. Keep plan IDs out of the workflow display `name:`; put them in comments/docs.
5. Never add a ghost `terraform.yml` workflow — lint/plan live in `CI: static analysis`.
